Feature Selection & Data Exploration Lab
This repository documents hands-on data analysis and feature engineering workflows in Python using Pandas, NumPy, and Seaborn.

Overview of Tasks
1. Filtering Out Highly Correlated Features (ansur_df)
When working with high-dimensional datasets (such as the 99-column numeric ANSUR dataset), multicollinearity can degrade model performance and introduce redundancy.

Correlation Matrix & Absolute Values: Computed the pairwise correlation matrix using .corr().abs().

Upper Triangle Masking: Generated a boolean mask using np.triu() and applied .mask() to isolate one half of the symmetric correlation matrix.

Feature Pruning: Automated the identification and removal of features with a correlation coefficient greater than 0.95, reducing dataset dimensionality while preserving core variance.

2. Spurious Correlations: Nuclear Energy & Pool Drownings (weird_df)
An exploration into statistical correlation versus causation using real-world data provided by the US Centers for Disease Control & Prevention and Department of Energy.

Data Inspection: Loaded and examined sample records tracking annual pool drownings alongside nuclear energy production metrics.

Data Visualization: Built scatterplots via Seaborn (sns.scatterplot) to visualize the apparent relationship.

